hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17154","Hajjaj and Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, Uthman said: freedman of al-Tawamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: We used to pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Maghrib, and go out to the market, and if one of us shot with an arrow, Uthman said: shot with arrows, he would see their sites."
"17155","Ibn Numayr and Yala and Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not take your houses as graves; pray in them."
"17156","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, and Yazid said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Amrah, that he heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, Yazid said: that Abu Amrah, freedman of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrate that a man of the Muslims died at Khaybar, and he was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Pray upon your companion. He said: The faces of the people changed at that. When he saw what was with them, he said: Your companion stole from the path of Allah. We searched his baggage and found in it beads of the Jews worth two dirhams."
"17157","Yala and Muhammad, sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not that I hardship, and Muhammad said: were it not that it is hardship upon my nation, I would delay the Isha prayer to a third of the night, and I would command them with the siwak at every prayer."
"17158","Yala narrated to us: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever breaks the fast of a fasting person, written for him is like his reward, except that it does not diminish of the reward of the fasting person anything. Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or succeeds him in his family, written for him is like his reward, except that it does not diminish of the reward of the warrior anything."
"17159","And Yazid said: He informed us, except that he said: without it being diminished."
"17160","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: A man cursed a rooster that crowed at the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not curse it, for it calls to prayer."
"17161","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Khalid, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in dawn at Hudaybiyah after rain. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"17162","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Ama inform, from a man called al-Saib, freedman of the Persians, and Ibn Bakr said: a freedman of Persia, and Hajjaj said: freedman of the Persians, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw him, and he was caliph, bow two rakahs after the Asr, and he walked to him and struck him with the stick while he was praying as he was. When he finished, Zayd said: O Commander of the Faithful, by Allah, I will never leave them after I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray them. He said: Umar sat to him and said: O Zayd ibn Khalid, were it not that I fear the people take them as a ladder to prayer until the night, I would not have struck about them."
"17163","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Khalid ibn Zayd al-Juhani, from his father Zayd ibn Khalid, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the stray of the shepherd of sheep. He said: It is for you or for the wolf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the stray of the shepherd of camels? He said: And what have you to do with it? With it are its water skin and its shoes, and it eats from the ends of the trees. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about silver when I find it? He said: Know its container and its tie and its number, then announce it a year. If its owner comes, pay it to him, else it is for you, or enjoy it, or like this."
"17164","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My son was a hireling with this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. They informed me that upon my son is stoning, so I ransomed from him with a slave girl and a hundred sheep. Then the people of knowledge informed me that upon my son is flogging a hundred and exile a year, and that upon the wife of this man is stoning. I reckoned he said: So judge between us by the Book of Allah. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I will judge between you by the Book of Allah. As for the sheep and the slave girl, they return to you. As for your son, upon him is flogging a hundred and exile a year. Then he said to a man of Aslam called Unays: Rise, O Unays, and ask the wife of this man; if she confesses, stone her."
"17165","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has raided, and whoever succeeds him has raided."
"17166","Ishaq ibn Isa informed us: Malik informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Abu Amrah al-Ansari, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, if Allah wills, Ishaq said: he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses, who brings the testimony before he is asked it."
"17167","Ibn al-Ashjai narrated to us, he said: My father, from Sufyan, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: I used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Maghrib, then go out to the market, and if I shot I would see the sites of my arrows."
"17168","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and Shibl, Sufyan said: Some people said: Ibn Mabad, and what I memorized: Shiblan, they said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man stood and said: I adjure you by Allah but you judge between us by the Book of Allah. His opponent stood, and he was more understanding than him, and said: He spoke truth; judge between us by the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and permit me to speak. He said: Say. He said: My son was a hireling with this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I ransomed from him with a hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked men of the people of knowledge, and they informed me that upon my son is flogging a hundred and exile a year, and upon the wife of this man is stoning. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I will judge between you by the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. The hundred sheep and the servant return to you, and upon your son is flogging a hundred and exile a year. Go in the morning, O Unays, a man of Aslam, to the wife of this man; if she confesses, stone her. He went in the morning to her, and she confessed, and he stoned her."
"17169","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid and Shibl, they said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a slave girl who commits adultery before she is muhsanah. He said: Flog her; if she returns, flog her; if she returns, flog her; if she returns, sell her even for a rope."
"17170","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not take your houses as graves; pray in them. Whoever breaks the fast of a fasting person, written for him is like the reward of the fasting person, nothing diminishing of the reward of the fasting person. Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or succeeds him in his family, written for him is like the reward of the warrior, in that nothing diminishes of the reward of the warrior anything."
"17171","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has raided, and whoever succeeds a warrior in his family with good has raided."
"17172","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about lost property. He said: Announce it a year. If it is recognized, pay it. Else know its container and its tie and its number. Else eat it. If it is recognized, pay it."
"17173","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umarah informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not inform you of the best of testimony, those who begin with their testimony without being asked about it."
"17174","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us, from Yahya: Abu Salamah narrated to us, and my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not that I hardship upon my nation, I would command them with the siwak at every prayer. He said: Zayd ibn Khalid would place the siwak from him at the position of the pen from the ear of the writer; whenever he stood to prayer, he used the siwak."
"17175","Sufyan narrated to us: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani: The people were rained upon at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night. In the morning they came, he said: Did you not hear what your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said tonight? He said: No blessing I bestow upon My servants but that thereby a people become disbelievers, through that which they believed in Me."
"17176","Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, Yahya said: Rabiah informed me that he said: from Zayd ibn Khalid. I asked Rabiah, and he said: He informed me, from Zayd ibn Khalid: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the stray camel, and he became angry and his cheeks reddened, and said: What have you to do with it? With it are the shoes and the water; it comes to water and eats trees until its owner comes. He was asked about the stray sheep, and said: Take it, for it is for you or for your brother or for the wolf. He was asked about lost property, and said: Know its container and its tie, then announce it a year. If it is recognized, else mix it with your wealth."
"17177","Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, freedman of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Mamar, from Busr ibn Said, he said: Abu Juhaym, son of the sister of Ubayy ibn Kab, sent me to Zayd ibn Khalid asking him what he heard about one passing before a praying person. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: For one to stand forty, I know not of a day or a month or a year, is better for him than to pass before him."
"17178","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: The freedman of al-Juhaynah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, narrating from his father, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid plunder and embezzlement."
"17179","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: We used to pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Maghrib, then go out to the market, and if shot with an arrow I would see its sites."
"17180","Abu Amir narrated to us: Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever performs wudu and perfects his wudu, then prays two rakahs not inattentive in them, Allah forgives him what preceded of his sin."
"17181","Yahya ibn Ishaq informed us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, and Surayj, he is Ibn al-Numan, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Abu Salim al-Jayshani, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever shelters a stray is astray unless he announces it."
"17182","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mubarak al-Hunai, Basran, trustworthy, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever equips a warrior has raided, and whoever succeeds him in his family has raided."
"17183","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a slave girl who commits adultery and is not muhsanah. He said: Flog her; if she commits adultery, flog her. He said at the third or at the fourth: If she commits adultery, sell her even for a rope. And the rope is the cord."
"17184","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, the meaning."
"17185","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a slave girl. Then he mentioned the hadith, and said at the third or the fourth, al-Zuhri doubted."
"17186","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, he said: Yazid, freedman of al-Munbaith, narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: A bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with lost property. He said: Announce it a year, then know its container and its tie. If one comes informing you of it, else spend it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and the stray sheep? He said: For you or for your brother or for the wolf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, the stray camel? He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed. Then he said: What have you to do with it? With it are its shoes and its water; it comes to water and eats trees."
"17187","He said: I read upon Abd al-Rahman: Malik, my father said, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in dawn at Hudaybiyah after rain that was in the night. When he finished, he turned to the people. He said: Do you know what your Lord said? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Some of My servants became a believer in Me, Ishaq said: a disbeliever in the star, and a believer in the star, a disbeliever in Me. As for one who said: We were rained by the grace of Allah and by His mercy, that is a believer in Me, a disbeliever in the star. As for one who said: We were rained by such-and-such star, that is a disbeliever in Me, a believer in the star."
"17188","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of testimony is one whose owner testifies with it before he is asked it."
